1
00:00:14,056 --> 00:00:16,141
[Madeline] What was Elise
even doing up here?

2
00:00:16,224 --> 00:00:19,144
[Simone] Who knows?
She was terrified of heights.

3
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:21,604
Wouldn't even take the top bunk
at summer camp.

4
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,231
[Madeline]
Someone must've brought her up here.

5
00:00:23,315 --> 00:00:24,566
Someone she trusted.

6
00:00:24,649 --> 00:00:25,692
[Pastor Lewis] Whoever it was,

7
00:00:25,775 --> 00:00:28,653
he really... let her down.

8
00:00:28,736 --> 00:00:31,031
And cut! Good enough. Thank you.

9
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:32,657
All right, that is lunch, folks.

10
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:34,784
But before you go
to get your carnitas, listen up.

11
00:00:34,867 --> 00:00:36,869
Can I get everybody
to gather around, please?

12
00:00:36,953 --> 00:00:39,747
Susan has some, uh,
important news she wants to share.

13
00:00:41,874 --> 00:00:43,835
-[Evan sighs]
-Is everything okay?

14
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:46,463
Susan's just gonna announce
she's taking us all to Disneyland.

15
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:47,630
Fuckin' idiot.

16
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:50,300
Hi, everyone. Uh...

17
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:53,386
Look, I'm just gonna, uh, get right to it.

18
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:56,723
Um, this morning I was told
that the network

19
00:00:56,806 --> 00:00:58,808
is cutting Witchita's episode order.

20
00:00:58,891 --> 00:01:00,310
[all exclaiming]

21
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:02,854
Yeah, they cut us from 16 to 12,

22
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:04,939
which means the episode
that we're shooting right now

23
00:01:05,022 --> 00:01:06,899
will be the last of the season.

24
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:10,278
And tomorrow will be
our last day of production.

25
00:01:10,362 --> 00:01:12,905
Why is this happening, Susan?
Did they say something?

26
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:15,742
Are they just gonna put on
another fuckin' reality show?

27
00:01:15,825 --> 00:01:19,871
Gina said it was due to low numbers
and they have a mid-season replacement

28
00:01:19,954 --> 00:01:22,874
with Calista Flockhart playing
some park ranger detective

29
00:01:22,957 --> 00:01:24,709
that's fuckin' testing through the roof.

30
00:01:24,792 --> 00:01:28,463
But... [takes deep breath]
listen, guys, this is not a cancellation.

31
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:32,008
It's a forced hiatus, and we will survive.

32
00:01:32,091 --> 00:01:34,427
Okay? Let's hold out hope
for another season.

33
00:01:35,803 --> 00:01:39,349
I mean, Witchita, you know,
we're more than a TV show.

34
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:42,602
[crying] We're a family, right?

35
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:43,811
Fuck! [chuckles]

36
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:46,022
Fuck, I'm fucking crying over Witchita.

37
00:01:46,105 --> 00:01:47,149
Shit.

38
00:01:50,152 --> 00:01:53,280
So what's this mean?
We canceled, or...

39
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:55,990
Let me put it this way.
I've been on three different shows,

40
00:01:56,073 --> 00:01:58,743
-all of them had their orders cut.
-[Rebecca] And what happened?

41
00:01:59,536 --> 00:02:01,788
[breath whooshes] All of them.

42
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:04,624
So this could be, like,
the last episode of Witchita ever?

43
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:08,670
-I mean, maybe I wrote the series finale.
-[Ali] Are you smiling?

44
00:02:08,753 --> 00:02:11,506
This isn't a birthday party.
It's a funeral.

45
00:02:11,589 --> 00:02:14,384
It's not a happy smile.
It's, like, a nervous smile.

46
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:16,136
When I found out my grandma died,
I laughed.

47
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:17,345
Fuck!

48
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:21,891
[sighs] Just bought a fucking Tesla!

49
00:02:21,974 --> 00:02:23,143
Now I'm fucked!

50
00:02:24,186 --> 00:02:25,312
[grunting] Fuck!

51
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:26,396
[Bertie] Randy...

52
00:02:26,479 --> 00:02:28,856
Mona... M-O-N-A-U?

53
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:31,776
Monahan. M-O-N-A-H-A-N.

54
00:02:31,859 --> 00:02:32,860
Oh.

55
00:02:35,738 --> 00:02:38,741
Wow.
This is amazing.

56
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:40,952
I'll totally pay you back at some point.
I swear.

57
00:02:41,035 --> 00:02:42,370
I'm impressed you can ask for help.

58
00:02:42,454 --> 00:02:43,663
Most guys couldn't do that.

59
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:45,873
Oh, wait, you forgot to sign it.

60
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:48,835
-Oh, my God. So stupid. Sorry.
-[chuckles]

61
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:51,170
-You gotta sign it or I can't cash it.
-Mmm-hmm.

62
00:02:53,506 --> 00:02:55,758
-Thank you, Bertie.
-You're welcome.

63
00:03:06,143 --> 00:03:08,145
[theme music playing]

64
00:03:31,586 --> 00:03:33,129
Hey, what are you doing here?

65
00:03:33,588 --> 00:03:35,632
-Hanging with Bertie.
-Oh, yeah?

66
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:38,718
Well, I think it's time to wrap this up

67
00:03:38,801 --> 00:03:41,012
'cause Bertie and I have
a whole mall day planned.

68
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:43,348
We went a little overboard
at the store at Topanga,

69
00:03:43,431 --> 00:03:45,141
and now we gotta return all this stuff.

70
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:47,269
Oh. I love that place.
Their dining terrace rules.

71
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:49,562
-Don't you mean food court?
-Uh, no.

72
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:52,649
At Topanga, it's a dining terrace.
It's super classy.

73
00:03:55,192 --> 00:03:57,194
Look, I don't mean to pry, but...

74
00:03:58,405 --> 00:04:00,365
don't you have a job
that you should be at?

75
