-Okay, I get it.

116
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:41,549
Sam already told me.
But how many weeks would they need me?

117
00:05:41,633 --> 00:05:43,468
Three weeks.
Maybe four.

118
00:05:43,551 --> 00:05:45,177
Shoots down in Atlanta.

119
00:05:45,261 --> 00:05:48,139
The president's daughter gets abducted,
and you play the president's daughter.

120
00:05:48,222 --> 00:05:50,767
Wow, Arya. That's very cool.

121
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:52,894
A big movie. Proud of ya.

122
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:55,522
And, uh, Mom, I'm guessing
you want me to do the indie one?

123
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:58,525
I do. I think Lowlands
is a better move for you.

124
00:05:58,608 --> 00:06:01,152
It's about a girl
whose mother is mentally ill.

125
00:06:01,235 --> 00:06:04,238
They're stranded in a snowstorm
without any medicine.

126
00:06:04,321 --> 00:06:06,866
And, Arya, the script made me cry.

127
00:06:06,949 --> 00:06:08,785
-You cry at GEICO commercials.
-[Denise] Steven.

128
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:11,663
Baby, this is an Oscar nom if you do well.

129
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:14,874
And, Arya, you would kill this role.

130
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:18,377
Liberty Down is a great movie.
It's gonna be on 4,000 screens.

131
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:20,713
Lowlands will be on one screen
in La Mirada.

132
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:22,882
Your friends can't get there
unless their parents drive them.

133
00:06:22,965 --> 00:06:25,384
-You're gonna be amazing... in Lowlands.
-You're a great little actress...

134
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:26,803
and you just pick one,

135
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:28,304
-and we'll be behind you.
-You'll be the star.

136
00:06:28,387 --> 00:06:29,764
[cell phone chimes]

137
00:06:29,847 --> 00:06:30,848
Oh.

138
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:35,186
Arya, they want you back on set,
so we should probably get going.

139
00:06:35,269 --> 00:06:36,854
Okay, we'll figure this out later.

140
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:38,022
-Scoot.
-Okay.

141
00:06:38,105 --> 00:06:39,231
[Gus] All right.

142
00:06:39,315 --> 00:06:40,316
[Denise] You look beautiful.

143
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:43,319
Do you think they have breakfast burritos?

144
00:06:44,612 --> 00:06:45,947
Fuck you. I'm hungry.

145
00:06:49,283 --> 00:06:53,496
All right, we're here,
and the store we need to go to is here.

146
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,748
Fuck. We parked on the wrong end.

147
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:57,459
Oh, well, silver lining,

148
00:06:57,542 --> 00:07:00,712
now we get to go see
the sights and sounds of Topanga.

149
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:04,966
Yeah, I need to make a pit stop
before we do the schlep.

150
00:07:05,049 --> 00:07:06,050
Okay.

151
00:07:07,259 --> 00:07:09,136
-Randy, we're peeing.
-Okay.

152
00:07:10,472 --> 00:07:11,681
Do these make me look cool?

153
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,684
How about these?

154
00:07:16,393 --> 00:07:18,062
-[toilet flushing]
-[Bertie] One of my goals is to take

155
00:07:18,145 --> 00:07:21,148
a more active role in decorating
our apartment, if that's cool with you.

156
00:07:21,232 --> 00:07:24,736
Oh, yeah.
I mean, mi casa es su casa.

157
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:28,405
It's kind of Randy's casa now too, huh?
Since he's there all the time.

158
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:31,033
How's it going with you guys?
Is it getting serious?

159
00:07:31,117 --> 00:07:32,452
I don't know. Maybe.

160
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:35,913
I'm trying not to think about it.
I just really wanna live in the moment,

161
00:07:35,997 --> 00:07:38,666
not think about the future at all.
Eckhart Tolle kind of thing.

162
00:07:38,750 --> 00:07:40,918
But wasn't he a little scary
when he was on shrooms

163
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:42,712
and he kept talking about killing people?

164
00:07:42,795 --> 00:07:45,965
Yeah. But then the next day,
he was just sweet, cuddly Randy again.

165
00:07:46,048 --> 00:07:48,801
So... yeah, I blame the mushrooms.

166
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:51,304
Okay. And you like him?

167
00:07:51,804 --> 00:07:54,265
Yeah. I love that he's so kind.

168
00:07:54,348 --> 00:07:58,227
And he has lot of free time, which is nice
at the beginning of a relationship.

169
00:07:58,310 --> 00:08:01,355
And I just like
that he likes being around me.

170
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:04,025
Mmm-hmm. Yeah.

171
00:08:04,108 --> 00:08:06,944
Don't you wish you were with somebody
who could take care of themselves?

172
00:08:07,028 --> 00:08:08,445
I mean, so many guys--

173
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:10,197
What makes you think
he can't take care of himself?

174
00:08:11,574 --> 00:08:15,703
So, like, you and Gus are going well,
and now you're a relationship expert?

175
00:08:16,538 --> 00:08:18,122
[sighs] Forget I said anything.

176
00:08:22,919 --> 00:08:25,087
Parfait? Parfait, anybody?

177
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:28,633
Parfait. Fresh banana.
Fruit. Kiwi. Berries.

178
00:08:28,716 --> 00:08:30,259
Treats by Kev. Just google it.

179
00:08:30,342 --> 00:08:31,886
I'm the man for any
of your catering needs.

180
00:08:31,969 --> 00:08:34,138
Anybody pregnant? I kill baby showers.

181
00:08:34,221 --> 00:08:35,682
Kevin, look at you!

182
00:08:35,765 --> 00:08:37,850
-Back to the hustle, huh?
-Dude, I gotta.

183
00:08:37,934 --> 00:08:40,019
How else am I gonna leave
a good impression?

184
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:41,478
-I know. I know.
-What about you?

185
00:08:41,563 --> 00:08:42,939
Shouldn't you be
sniffing around for another gig?

186
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:45,566
Oh. No, no, no, no. I, uh...

187
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:47,777
I think I know
what my next job's gonna be.

188
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:51,781
Arya's got a couple of movie offers,
so... knock on wood. [chuckles]

189
00:08:51,864 --> 00:08:52,698
God damn it, man.

190
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:55,076
I wish I had a nice little white girl
to hang out with.

191
00:08:55,159 --> 00:08:58,037
Well, everybody needs
a little white girl, right?

192
00:08:59,038 --> 00:09:01,958
I don't know.
I don't necessarily mean that.

193
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:04,168
-Hey. Hey, guys.
-Hey.

194
00:09:04,251 --> 00:09:06,337
-Hey, can I talk to you for one second?
-Yeah.

195
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:07,589
Sure. Totally.

196
00:09:07,672 --> 00:09:09,799
By the way, these things are unreal.
They're great.

197
00:09:09,882 --> 00:09:11,718
Dude, spread the word.
Treats by Kev, bro.

198
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:13,720
-Thank you. Let everybody know.
-[chuckles]

199
00:09:13,803 --> 00:09:15,137
-All right, man.
-Thank you.

200
00:09:15,847 --> 00:09:21,060
I hope this isn't weird, but, uh...
did I see you in an episode of Homicide?

201
00:09:21,143 --> 00:09:22,353
It was, like, Season 4.

202
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:24,271
-At the wedding.
-The one where the guy got arrested

203
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:25,690
-at his wedding.
-Yeah. Yeah.

204
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:28,442
-Oh, you were great. Yeah.
-Oh, man, thank you. That's great.

205
00:09:28,525 --> 00:09:30,695
You know, I never wanted Arya
to be an actor.

206
00:09:30,778 --> 00:09:32,614
Really? She's so good.

207
00:09:32,697 --> 00:09:34,031
Oh, she's fucking great.

208
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:37,076
But even if you're great, are you really
gonna be the next Meryl Streep?

209
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:38,744
-I mean, what are the chances?
-Yeah.

210
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:43,040
Spend her days like all of us,
out there getting rejected

211
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:45,877
and holding out hope
for that one big payday.

212
00:09:46,794 --> 00:09:49,296
Then Liberty Down falls in her lap.
It's, like, a franchise.

213
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:51,382
-I don't... I don't know.
-I know. It's so cool.

214
00:09:51,465 --> 00:09:52,508
It's crazy.

215
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:54,886
She does one movie, works for a decade.

216
00:09:54,969 --> 00:09:56,846
She could pay her way through college.

217
00:09:57,722 --> 00:10:00,141
-Yeah. I didn't realize.
-Yeah.

218
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:03,394
Denise doesn't think like that either.

219
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:06,022
-Can you sit down for a sec?
-Yeah.

220
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:08,691
[grunting]

221
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:11,861
I, uh...

222
00:10:13,195 --> 00:10:15,364
I don't think anybody knows this,
but, um...

223
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:17,617
we're getting a divorce.

224
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,160
-Oh...
-Yeah.

225
00:10:19,243 --> 00:10:22,538
Jeez, man, that... that sucks.
I'm... I'm sorry to hear that.

226
00:10:23,122 --> 00:10:27,043
I just get a little worried that I won't
have any say in my daughter's future.

227
00:10:27,126 --> 00:10:28,127
Mmm-hmm.

228
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:30,046
You're on set with Denise. You get it.

229
00:10:30,129 --> 00:10:31,505
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah.

230
00:10:31,588 --> 00:10:32,757
She can be intimidating.

231
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:33,799
Yeah, she's a cunt.

232
00:10:35,009 --> 00:10:37,386
You've only done one season with her.
I've done 14.

233
00:10:37,469 --> 00:10:39,221
[chuckles] Yeah.

234
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:40,472
-It's brutal.
-Yeah.

235
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:42,600
But poor Arya. You know what I mean?

236
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:45,477
Her show gets shit-canned, uh...

237
00:10:45,561 --> 00:10:48,522
Her parents are getting a divorce.
That's a drag.

238
00:10:48,605 --> 00:10:50,733
Well, hey, if there's anything
I can do to help,

239
00:10:50,817 --> 00:10:53,110
or whatever, you know, I'm here.

240
00:10:53,736 --> 00:10:57,239
Just talk to her.
Be a good influence.

241
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:59,366
-She likes you. She says she likes you.
-Yeah?

242
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:01,327
-Yeah.
-Aw, that's sweet.

243
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:03,746
And I think we both agree
that Liberty Down

244
00:11:03,830 --> 00:11:05,665
is probably the best move
for her right now.

245
00:11:06,290 --> 00:11:08,876
Yeah. All right, I'm gonna scoot.

246
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,419
-[sighs]
-Oh, okay.

247
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:14,048
Can I give you this?

248
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:15,758
-Sure.
-Thanks.

249
00:11:17,009 --> 00:11:18,845
[cell phone vibrating]

250
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:22,974
Hello? Cynthia?

251
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:24,183
It's Cynthia from work.

252
00:11:24,266 --> 00:11:26,643
Cynthia, can you hear me?
I'm in a mall.

253
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:28,354
A mall!

254
00:11:28,437 --> 00:11:31,565
Did you know that the people who build
malls put the escalators at either end

255
00:11:31,648 --> 00:11:34,443
so that you got to walk
by all the shops to get to 'em?

256
00:11:34,526 --> 00:11:37,404
-You know a lot about malls.
-[Bertie] Oh, no. Really?

257
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:39,323
Yeah.
Malls and casinos.

258
00:11:39,406 --> 00:11:41,909
You guys, I'm so sorry,
but I'm gonna have to go in to work.

259
00:11:41,993 --> 00:11:42,994
Right now?

260
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:45,747
Yeah, well, Cynthia... Cynthia's
from work, and she's got the flu,

261
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:48,665
and she was meant to be running
a microwave popcorn focus group today,

262
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:50,626
but now I'm gonna have
to go cover for her.

263
00:11:50,709 --> 00:11:52,128
-Crap.
-[Randy] Go.

264
00:11:52,211 --> 00:11:54,546
-Mickey and I can do the returns.
-Really?

265
00:11:54,630 --> 00:11:57,716
-You'd do that for me?
-Of course. Anything for Bertie.

266
00:11:59,135 --> 00:12:00,386
You okay with that, Mickey?

267
00:12:01,428 --> 00:12:04,598
Yeah. I'm just wondering
how we're gonna get back without your car.

268
00:12:04,681 --> 00:12:07,393
We can Uber.
You have an account, right, Mickey?

269
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:08,602
Um...

270
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:11,688
-Yeah...
-[Bertie] Okay, great!

271
00:12:11,773 --> 00:12:14,691
I think this will be good.
You two are gonna have fun together.

272
00:12:14,776 --> 00:12:15,943
Okay.

273
00:12:16,027 --> 00:12:17,611
Sorry. Thank you.

274
00:12:17,694 --> 00:12:18,821
See ya.

275
00:12:21,866 --> 00:12:22,867
Bye!

276
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:25,161
Bye, Bertie.

277
00:12:26,662 --> 00:12:28,831
-You wanna get something to eat?
-No.

278
00:12:28,915 --> 00:12:31,208
How about, like, a pretzel or something?
Something quick.

279
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:33,252
-[cashier] And you're all set.
-[Mickey] Thanks.

280
00:12:33,335 --> 00:12:35,504
My roommate and I
went a little crazy the other day.

281
00:12:39,591 --> 00:12:40,968
[sighs] Cool, right?

282
00:12:41,052 --> 00:12:43,179
What are you gonna do
with a filing cabinet?

283
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:44,721
You can put anything in there.

284
00:12:44,806 --> 00:12:49,060
You can put clothes and paper and food,
if you want. And it's really cute.

285
00:12:49,143 --> 00:12:51,395
[cashier] That'll be $39.99.

286
00:12:51,478 --> 00:12:52,521
Oh!

287
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:55,817
-[Randy] Thanks.
-[cashier] Debit or credit?

288
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:58,235
[Randy] Credit, please.
It's my first real piece of furniture.

289
00:12:58,319 --> 00:13:00,529
-And you're all set.
-[Randy] Thanks so much.

290
00:13:00,612 --> 00:13:03,991
I think I'm gonna put it
right in my living room.

291
00:13:04,075 --> 00:13:05,451
It looks like R2-D2.

292
00:13:05,534 --> 00:13:06,953
-[imitating R2-D2]
-[Mickey] No.

293
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:11,207
-Arya?
-Gus!

294
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:13,709
-Oh. Hey.
-Hey.

295
00:13:13,792 --> 00:13:16,087
-Arya's not here.
-Okay, I'll just... I'll come back later.

296
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:17,629
Uh, no, no, no. Nope, come here.

297
00:13:17,713 --> 00:13:20,132
-I need to talk to you for a second.
-All right. Okay.

298
00:13:21,258 --> 00:13:22,468
-Look...
-What's up?

299
00:13:22,551 --> 00:13:25,972
I am really sorry about all that craziness
that you witnessed this morning.

300
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:27,639
-That was... You know.
-Oh...

301
00:13:27,723 --> 00:13:30,517
No, that's okay.
I understand how that stuff goes.

302
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:34,939
And I think you should finally know
that Steve and I are splitting up.

303
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:38,359
-Oh. I'm sorry to hear that.
-Yeah.

304
00:13:38,442 --> 00:13:39,986
-No, well...
-[stammers] That's a shame.

305
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:41,612
I mean, we were not really a great fit.

306
00:13:41,695 --> 00:13:44,406
Ahh, no, I feel like you guys,
you know, started dating,

307
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:46,033
you got married, right?

308
00:13:46,117 --> 00:13:48,244
Come on, we were young.
We were having a great time.

309
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:49,411
The sex was...

310
00:13:49,495 --> 00:13:53,332
Oh, well, we don't need
to get into all that...

311
00:13:53,415 --> 00:13:54,583
-Yeah, well...
-right now.

312
00:13:54,666 --> 00:13:56,752
every time that I tried
to break up with him...

313
00:13:56,835 --> 00:13:59,338
-Mmm-hmm?
-[sighs] ...he would get me so...

314
00:14:00,256 --> 00:14:01,090
I mean...

315
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:04,301
you know, like, hard.

316
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:07,221
-And it was... I mean...
-Mmm. Mmm-hmm. Mmm.

317
00:14:07,304 --> 00:14:08,973
-Mmm-hmm.
-beyond.

318
00:14:09,056 --> 00:14:11,017
-Yeah. No, that's romantic.
-And he still does.

319
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,809
-[chuckles]
-Oh. That's sweet.

320
00:14:12,894 --> 00:14:14,896
But everything else
is a fucking nightmare.

321
00:14:14,979 --> 00:14:16,981
-Mmm-hmm.
-I mean, you cannot raise a child

322
00:14:17,064 --> 00:14:18,274
with a man like that.

323
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:20,109
-You know? No.
-I imagine not. Uh...

324
00:14:20,192 --> 00:14:21,944
So do you know where Arya went, or...

325
00:14:22,028 --> 00:14:24,488
Oh, please don't tell Arya anything, okay?

326
00:14:24,571 --> 00:14:25,865
-Oh.
-She doesn't know anything

327
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:27,241
-about the divorce yet.
-No, don't--

328
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:29,243
-Not a word. Okay.
-Yeah, I won't say anything.

329
00:14:29,326 --> 00:14:31,162
I have a favor.

330
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:32,288
All right.

331
00:14:32,371 --> 00:14:34,373
-Lowlands.
-Okay.

332
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:38,335
-Liberty Down.
-Ah. All right.

333
00:14:38,419 --> 00:14:40,504
So Arya trusts you.

334
00:14:40,587 --> 00:14:43,049
-Mmm.
-I want you to read both of those

335
00:14:43,132 --> 00:14:45,842
and just let Arya know what you think.

336
00:14:45,927 --> 00:14:47,887
I think you'll see what I mean.

337
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:49,013
Yeah.

338
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:51,223
Um, okay. I just...

339
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:53,392
I'm a little worried
it's a busy day today.

340
00:14:53,475 --> 00:14:54,643
The last day of production and all.

341
00:14:54,726 --> 00:14:57,688
So I don't know if I can dig into these,
like, right now. But--

342
00:14:57,771 --> 00:14:59,356
-Gus?
-Mmm-hmm?

343
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:02,026
You can do this for me.
For us.

344
00:15:02,944 --> 00:15:04,946
Okay, uh...

345
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:06,989
Yeah. No, I... Let me get at it.
I'd be happy to.

346
00:15:07,073 --> 00:15:08,699
-Good. Yes, thank you.
-It'll be great.

347
00:15:08,782 --> 00:15:10,076
-Great.
-Okay.

348
00:15:12,578 --> 00:15:15,497
[sighs] There it is.
The dining terrace. Let's go.

349
00:15:15,581 --> 00:15:19,543
No. Dude, I'm hungry, too,
but I'm so tired. I want to go home.

350
00:15:19,626 --> 00:15:22,338
My blood sugar's low.
I... I really need to eat right now.

351
00:15:22,421 --> 00:15:24,381
-It's bad if I don't eat.
-Can we eat at home?

352
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:25,591
It's cheaper anyway.

353
00:15:25,674 --> 00:15:27,884
[sighs] I hate home food.

354
00:15:27,969 --> 00:15:29,553
What? That's normal.

355
00:15:29,636 --> 00:15:32,889
Now who's gonna pay for this
dining terrace food, by the way?

356
00:15:32,974 --> 00:15:34,558
-I am.
-Oh, really?

357
00:15:34,641 --> 00:15:37,269
Or is Bertie?
'Cause I know that she lent you money.

358
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:41,523
-She told you that?
-No. I saw it. Or I heard it.

359
00:15:42,691 --> 00:15:45,402
Dude, you're in my house.
You're always in my fuckin' house.

360
00:15:45,486 --> 00:15:46,820
How much money did she give you?

361
00:15:48,572 --> 00:15:49,573
How much?

362
00:15:50,532 --> 00:15:52,284
$850. It's for my rent.

363
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:53,869
$850?

364
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:55,912
I thought she gave you, like, 100 bucks.

365
00:15:55,997 --> 00:15:58,749
And you took it?
What the fuck's wrong with you?

366
00:15:58,832 --> 00:15:59,875
Nothing's wrong with me.

367
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:02,253
Really? 'Cause you're 30,
and you don't have a job.

368
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:05,422
Bertie just got here from Australia,
and now you're gonna bleed her dry?

369
00:16:05,506 --> 00:16:07,341
-No, I'm not.
-Really?

370
00:16:07,424 --> 00:16:08,925
I like Bertie.
She's my friend.

371
00:16:09,010 --> 00:16:11,053
Well, you're runnin' a nice scam
on her right now.

372
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:14,181
-It's not a fuckin' scam, Mickey.
-It is a scam.

373
00:16:14,265 --> 00:16:15,516
And I know it 'cause I've done it.

374
00:16:15,599 --> 00:16:17,684
You don't think I've gotten guys
to pay my rent?

375
00:16:17,768 --> 00:16:20,521
I dated one dude, I got him to buy me
all these expensive clothes.

376
00:16:20,604 --> 00:16:22,606
I'd just e-mail him links,
and he'd buy me the shit.

377
00:16:22,689 --> 00:16:24,983
Well, it's not my fault, okay?

378
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:28,279
I get these little side jobs, but it's
hard to hold down a job full-time.

379
00:16:28,362 --> 00:16:30,739
And there's no jobs left
in this fucking country anyway.

380
00:16:30,822 --> 00:16:32,241
Ask anybody here!

381
00:16:32,324 --> 00:16:36,787
Oh, really? 'Cause that person has a job.
Job, job, job, job, job!

382
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:39,956
You're literally surrounded by jobs.
What's your excuse?

383
00:16:40,041 --> 00:16:42,084
-Fine!
-Where are you going?

384
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:44,670
I'm gonna go get a job,

385
00:16:44,753 --> 00:16:47,214
because it's so freakin' easy
to get, right?

386
00:16:47,298 --> 00:16:48,924
Yeah, it is.

387
00:16:49,007 --> 00:16:51,010
You look so stupid wheeling that thing.

388
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:01,812
Hey. Can I help you?

389
00:17:01,895 --> 00:17:03,314
Yeah, cool store.

390
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:04,981
I like the stuff you guys sell here.

391
00:17:05,066 --> 00:17:09,028
It's, uh, very sophisticated.
Uh, so are you guys, like, hiring?

392
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:11,572
Oh, not right now.
We just hired someone, so...

393
00:17:11,655 --> 00:17:13,865
Guess you're out of luck.
Can we go, please?

394
00:17:13,949 --> 00:17:15,451
Can I talk to a manager or something?

395
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:18,037
I'd really like to have a job today,
if possible.

396
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,456
Yeah, sorry. Um, the manager's not here.
[chuckles]

397
00:17:20,539 --> 00:17:23,334
Okay, but she says
that there are jobs everywhere.

398
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:25,711
And, uh, you know,
I know a lot about selling stuff,

399
00:17:25,794 --> 00:17:26,920
and I'm a great team player.

400
00:17:27,003 --> 00:17:28,589
Do you have any retail experience?

401
00:17:28,672 --> 00:17:30,841
I sell my plasma sometimes, so...

402
00:17:30,924 --> 00:17:32,218
Yeah, that doesn't count.

403
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:35,762
Um, this job is about, um, personality.

404
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:37,806
[scoffs] Well,
I have an awesome personality.

405
00:17:37,889 --> 00:17:39,266
People tell me that all the time.

406
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:41,435
They say, "Randy,
your personality fuckin' rocks!"

407
00:17:41,518 --> 00:17:43,145
Okay. You made your point, all right?

408
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:45,021
Okay, can I just leave my e-mail
and my name?

409
00:17:45,106 --> 00:17:47,983
And then when a job opens up later,
you contact me and I come in.

410
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:49,443
Uh, I don't think so, man. Sorry.

411
00:17:49,526 --> 00:17:51,945
Please. I can sell these little
funeral clothes to kids, okay?

412
00:17:52,028 --> 00:17:53,989
It's not for funerals.
Kids don't wear these to funerals.

413
00:17:54,072 --> 00:17:57,201
Then what do they wear these clothes for?
To get beat the shit out of in school?

414
00:17:57,284 --> 00:17:58,202
Please leave.

415
00:17:58,702 --> 00:18:00,162
-Oh, my God!
-Whoa. Come on, dude.

416
00:18:00,246 --> 00:18:01,580
-Oh, dude. Come on.
-We'll go when I'm ready.

417
00:18:01,663 --> 00:18:03,790
-What are you doing?
-I hate this store and I hate you.

418
00:18:03,874 --> 00:18:05,376
You know how long it takes
to arrange those things?

419
00:18:05,459 --> 00:18:07,002
No, because I don't fuckin' work here!

420
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:08,545
[Mickey] We're going! Come on!

421
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:10,089
You're gonna regret this, man.

422
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:12,549
You're gonna regret
not hiring Randy Farquaad.

423
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:13,925
I... Oh, come on, dude.

424
00:18:14,009 --> 00:18:15,511
-Now you showed him.
-Have fun picking it up.

425
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:17,304
Don't tell him your name, you idiot!

426
00:18:17,388 --> 00:18:20,099
That's not my name.
It's the evil prince from Shrek.

427
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:25,896
Yeah.

428
00:18:26,813 --> 00:18:28,607
No, I'm still here.

429
00:18:28,690 --> 00:18:29,733
No.

430
00:18:29,816 --> 00:18:31,360
I'm not wearing this dress.

431
00:18:31,443 --> 00:18:33,612
But you were wearing it
in the first part of the scene.

432
00:18:33,695 --> 00:18:34,946
The part we already shot.

433
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,323
[Arya] It makes me look old.

434
00:18:36,407 --> 00:18:38,534
-Why can't I just wear that one?
-That's Heidi's.

435
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:41,662
Well, uh, her character's dead.
Why can't it just be mine?

436
00:18:41,745 --> 00:18:43,247
No, Arya, it can't be yours.

437
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:46,375
Now, listen, you know how this works.
It's a continuity thing.

438
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:47,793
I'm not putting it on.

439
00:18:47,876 --> 00:18:50,504
You're gonna put that dress on.
You're gonna shoot your final scene.

440
00:18:50,587 --> 00:18:52,173
You're gonna rock it.
And then once you're done,

441
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:54,883
you can just go off
and do whatever you want. Okay?

442
00:18:55,717 --> 00:18:56,927
[whispers] I hate this place.

443
00:18:57,010 --> 00:18:59,054
-[Gus] Sorry about them cutting the order.
-Don't even...

444
00:19:00,305 --> 00:19:01,306
Hey, Arya.

445
00:19:02,391 --> 00:19:04,101
You decided what movie you wanna do?

446
00:19:04,601 --> 00:19:05,894
Nope. [sighs]

447
00:19:07,313 --> 00:19:08,355
See, now...

448
00:19:09,064 --> 00:19:12,401
I was flipping through these scripts,
and I gotta say Lowlands is pretty good.

449
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:14,320
Are you kidding me?
They're both awful.

450
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:17,531
One's a mindless action movie,
and one's a derivative indie.

451
00:19:17,614 --> 00:19:19,115
They both suck my ass.

452
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:22,286
All right. That's...
an astute way of putting it.

453
00:19:22,369 --> 00:19:24,705
I was just reading them,
you know, 'cause...

454
00:19:24,788 --> 00:19:28,625
I don't know. I'm worried about you
with Witchita ending, right?

455
00:19:28,709 --> 00:19:30,085
You must be freaked out.

456
00:19:30,168 --> 00:19:33,464
I could not care less.
I've always hated it here.

457
00:19:34,798 --> 00:19:38,344
-Well, what would you wanna do next?
-I don't know.

458
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:42,055
Be a normal kid.
Go to school. Have a boyfriend.

459
00:19:42,138 --> 00:19:43,724
I should be smoking and making out,

460
00:19:43,807 --> 00:19:46,477
not standing here
with a bunch of 50-year-olds all day.

461
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:48,103
[Evan] Hey, Arya.

462
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:49,771
Like him.

463
00:19:49,855 --> 00:19:51,147
Why do I know him?

464
00:19:52,691 --> 00:19:55,527
Okay. I see where you're coming from.

465
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:57,488
I get how it'd be a bummer for you, okay?

466
00:19:59,030 --> 00:20:00,241
Nobody cares what I think.

467
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:03,952
Hey, I care what you feel, okay?
Don't say that.

468
00:20:04,035 --> 00:20:05,036
No, you don't.

469
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:06,913
You just want me to work
so you have a job.

470
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:09,916
Hey, I could get a job without you, okay?

471
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:14,045
I just prefer to have a job with you,
'cause you're cool, all right?

472
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:17,257
But you should do what you want, okay?

473
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:19,843
Whatever you decide,
I'll... I'll support you.

474
00:20:19,926 --> 00:20:23,389
Well, if I don't support my parents,
they're gonna go bankrupt.

475
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:25,015
They're always fighting about money.

476
00:20:25,098 --> 00:20:26,975
Well, your parents can be a little cuckoo,

477
00:20:27,058 --> 00:20:29,895
but... if you told them
what you just told me,

478
00:20:29,978 --> 00:20:31,522
they'd be cool with it.
Promise.

479
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:32,773
Or...

480
00:20:34,065 --> 00:20:35,276
you could tell them.

481
00:20:35,984 --> 00:20:37,944
I don't know,
'cause I kind of feel like

482
00:20:38,028 --> 00:20:40,531
if you did it,
it'd be a good learning experience.

483
00:20:40,614 --> 00:20:43,450
You'd learn how to fight your own battles.
I don't need that experience.

484
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:45,994
Come on, I'm paying you.
You can do at least one thing.

485
00:20:46,703 --> 00:20:47,871
Besides educate you?

486
00:20:48,497 --> 00:20:50,457
Well, that's obviously not working.

487
00:21:52,018 --> 00:21:54,938
So, uh... I know why you don't like me.

488
00:21:55,021 --> 00:21:57,065
I... I know I'm pathetic.

489
00:21:57,148 --> 00:21:58,734
The thing is, I really like Bertie.

490
00:21:58,817 --> 00:22:00,736
She's so funny and hot...

491
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:02,863
doesn't mind having me around.

492
00:22:03,739 --> 00:22:05,657
I think I borrowed money from her

493
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:08,410
because I know I'm gonna
fuck things up sooner or later.

494
00:22:08,494 --> 00:22:11,037
So... might as well be sooner.

495
00:22:14,666 --> 00:22:15,876
Nah, dude.

496
00:22:17,669 --> 00:22:18,962
Me, too.

497
00:22:19,045 --> 00:22:21,673
I'm worried I'm gonna fuck up things
with Gus every single day.

498
00:22:23,175 --> 00:22:24,342
What if I fall off the wagon?

499
00:22:25,802 --> 00:22:29,264
Or I do something crazy?
Or I'm impulsive, or...

500
00:22:29,723 --> 00:22:33,018
I mean, he wants me to get better
so badly, but what if I can't?

501
00:22:33,101 --> 00:22:35,353
You know? I mean, I...
I fuck everything up.

502
00:22:35,437 --> 00:22:37,398
So why not Gus, too, right?

503
00:22:37,481 --> 00:22:40,191
Well... you never know.

504
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:45,196
This time, maybe Gus does something
really dumb and ruins everything.

505
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:46,322
[chuckles]

506
00:22:46,407 --> 00:22:49,117
-He can be a real idiot sometimes, so...
-That's true.

507
00:22:50,994 --> 00:22:52,245
Or maybe nobody will screw up,

508
00:22:52,328 --> 00:22:54,915
and you guys will be happy
for a long time.

509
00:22:55,499 --> 00:22:56,958
-It could happen.
-That'd be cool.

510
00:23:06,677 --> 00:23:08,429
Here. You...
you can give this back to her.

511
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:10,847
I... I don't deserve that.

512
00:23:14,518 --> 00:23:16,978
It's okay.
She wanted you to have it.

513
00:23:28,490 --> 00:23:29,908
[Steven] You won't let me
in her life.

514
00:23:29,991 --> 00:23:31,493
You don't let me in her account.

515
00:23:31,577 --> 00:23:32,828
I can't call her agent.

516
00:23:32,911 --> 00:23:33,954
-No.
-I'm not allowed.

517
00:23:34,037 --> 00:23:35,539
I am the one that does everything for her.

518
00:23:35,622 --> 00:23:36,957
[Steven] That still
doesn't answer the question.

519
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:38,041
-I'm fine--
-[stammers]

520
00:23:38,124 --> 00:23:39,209
-Hey.
-Oh, my God.

521
00:23:39,292 --> 00:23:41,503
-Is it a good time?
-[Steven] Not really.

522
00:23:41,587 --> 00:23:42,754
Never is, right? [chuckles]

523
00:23:43,755 --> 00:23:45,591
Okay, so here's the thing.

524
00:23:45,674 --> 00:23:48,677
Um, talked about it with Arya,

525
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:51,179
and we decided
that the best thing for her to do

526
00:23:51,262 --> 00:23:53,389
after Witchita is...

527
00:23:53,473 --> 00:23:54,307
[inhales]

528
00:23:55,225 --> 00:23:56,226
nothing.

529
00:23:56,309 --> 00:23:58,353
She doesn't want to do either movie.

530
00:23:58,436 --> 00:24:00,146
She just wants
to take a break from acting,

531
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:03,400
and, um, you know,
I think she just wants to be a kid again.

532
00:24:04,359 --> 00:24:05,944
And maybe...

533
00:24:06,027 --> 00:24:10,323
it's sort of our job to do the right thing
and look out for her.

534
00:24:13,410 --> 00:24:16,079
Arya, is this something you really want?

535
00:24:16,162 --> 00:24:17,413
Yes.

536
00:24:19,040 --> 00:24:20,083
Okay, then.

537
00:24:21,001 --> 00:24:22,002
I'm okay with that.

538
00:24:22,085 --> 00:24:24,505
Great. Yeah, I think
this will be good for everybody.

539
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:25,881
In fact, it's perfect.

540
00:24:25,964 --> 00:24:28,925
I mean, Lowlands doesn't start
shooting for another three weeks.

541
00:24:29,009 --> 00:24:31,052
We can... we can go to Hawaii.

542
00:24:31,136 --> 00:24:34,055
We can get mud baths,
get totally blissed out.

543
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:36,016
And then you can come back,
and we'll be so relaxed.

544
00:24:36,099 --> 00:24:37,392
-And--
-Are you serious?

545
00:24:38,309 --> 00:24:39,811
-What?
-She's not doing Lowlands!

546
00:24:39,895 --> 00:24:42,272
She just said she doesn't want to work.
Are you stupid?

547
00:24:42,355 --> 00:24:44,149
The kid says, "I need a break,"

548
00:24:44,232 --> 00:24:45,817
and you come up with that shit?

549
00:24:45,901 --> 00:24:47,569
[Denise] You decide
to parent for one day

550
00:24:47,653 --> 00:24:51,281
-and you think you know what's best?
-Well, because you don't let me near her.

551
00:24:51,364 --> 00:24:52,448
Why don't you let me near her?

552
00:24:52,533 --> 00:24:55,410
Are you worried that I might see
all the scamming and scheming

553
00:24:55,493 --> 00:24:56,995
-as you steal all her money?
-Oh, no--

554
00:24:57,078 --> 00:24:58,830
God! Shut up!

555
00:24:58,914 --> 00:25:02,584
Stop! I know what's going on.
I know you're getting a divorce.

556
00:25:02,668 --> 00:25:04,002
God damn it, Gus. Really?

557
00:25:04,085 --> 00:25:05,546
Are you serious? He didn't tell me!

558
00:25:05,629 --> 00:25:08,882
I can hear you guys! I'm not stupid!

559
00:25:08,965 --> 00:25:10,551
I heard you. I heard both of you.

560
00:25:10,634 --> 00:25:11,885
[sighs]

561
00:25:11,968 --> 00:25:14,429
[stammers] Honey, listen.

562
00:25:14,512 --> 00:25:18,058
Obviously, we love you so much.
It's nothing to do with you.

563
00:25:18,141 --> 00:25:20,727
And if it were up to me,
I would have told you months ago.

564
00:25:20,811 --> 00:25:23,104
Oh, my God, are you really
trying to score points with--

565
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:25,190
Will you shut up? Shut up!

566
00:25:25,273 --> 00:25:27,108
I don't even know
what we're arguing about.

567
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:30,070
Just tell Sam that I'll do both.
We'll figure something out.

568
00:25:30,153 --> 00:25:33,448
You can come with me to Liberty,
and you can come with me to Lowlands.

569
00:25:33,531 --> 00:25:35,366
Okay? And Gus can come to both

570
00:25:35,450 --> 00:25:38,161
to teach me the stupid shit
I don't need to know.

571
00:25:38,244 --> 00:25:39,580
Are you satisfied?

572
00:25:41,873 --> 00:25:42,874
I'm cool with that.

573
00:25:42,958 --> 00:25:44,375
-[Denise] Fine.
-Done! Go!

574
00:25:54,427 --> 00:25:56,429
I guess you have two jobs now, dipshit.

575
00:26:01,059 --> 00:26:02,143
Thank you.

576
00:26:06,564 --> 00:26:08,859
-Bertie, Bertie, what's up?
-Hey, how are you?

577
00:26:08,942 --> 00:26:10,026
-How you doin'?
-I'm good.

578
00:26:10,110 --> 00:26:11,194
They stuck you with the popcorn?

579
00:26:11,277 --> 00:26:13,154
Yeah, the most boring possible thing,
right?

580
00:26:13,238 --> 00:26:14,615
-That sucks.
-What you got today?

581
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:16,032
Um, juicers.

582
00:26:16,116 --> 00:26:17,283
So dumb.

583
00:26:17,367 --> 00:26:18,869
I thought you had the day off today.

584
00:26:18,952 --> 00:26:20,871
Oh, yeah, but Cynthia
asked me to cover for her.

585
00:26:20,954 --> 00:26:22,956
-She's got the flu.
-Cynthia?

586
00:26:23,039 --> 00:26:25,125
She just posted,
like, six pictures on Instagram

587
00:26:25,208 --> 00:26:26,960
from the Wizarding World of Harry Potter.

588
00:26:27,544 --> 00:26:31,172
Yeah, she ridin' rides,
playing Quidditch, drinkin' butterbeer.

589
00:26:31,256 --> 00:26:32,548
Oh, man, hold on.

590
00:26:32,633 --> 00:26:36,302
So you mean she's out there having fun,
and you're here stuck doing popcorn?

591
00:26:36,386 --> 00:26:39,180
Oh, man.
She took you for a ride.

592
00:26:40,181 --> 00:26:41,516
Why would she do that to me?

593
00:26:42,558 --> 00:26:44,811
Probably because you always say yes.

594
00:26:44,895 --> 00:26:46,312
No, I don't. Do I?

595
00:26:46,396 --> 00:26:49,232
-Bertie, you're a total pushover.
-I'm not a pushover!

596
00:26:49,315 --> 00:26:51,526
I mean it in a good way.
That's why we like you.

597
00:26:51,609 --> 00:26:53,945
You... you do what people ask you to.
You're great.

598
00:26:54,946 --> 00:26:57,282
Well, she's a bitch! That's right.

599
00:26:57,365 --> 00:26:59,367
I'm sorry to say it,
but that's what Cynthia is,

600
00:26:59,450 --> 00:27:00,702
and I think we can all agree.

601
00:27:00,786 --> 00:27:04,372
I don't need a focus group to tell me
that Cynthia's a royal fucking bitch!

602
00:27:04,455 --> 00:27:05,707
Do you like Cynthia?

603
00:27:05,791 --> 00:27:07,793
Uh, I mean, she's... No... no--

604
00:27:07,876 --> 00:27:10,628
No, I don't think you do, because
she's a total fucking bitch, right?

605
00:27:10,712 --> 00:27:11,797
And guess what?

606
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,381
She's never even read Harry Potter.

607
00:27:13,464 --> 00:27:15,091
I've read it. I've read them all twice.

608
00:27:15,175 --> 00:27:17,552
That's seven books twice.
That's 14 books.

609
00:27:17,635 --> 00:27:20,471
She's never even read it.
She's not even enjoying the park.

610
00:27:21,682 --> 00:27:24,309
[sighs] Good luck with the juicers.

611
00:27:24,392 --> 00:27:25,393
Okay.

612
00:27:29,815 --> 00:27:32,150
You Mickey? I'm your Uber driver.

613
00:27:40,325 --> 00:27:41,534
[sighs]

614
00:27:41,617 --> 00:27:44,079
Actually, uh,
I think I'll stick around here.

615
00:27:44,663 --> 00:27:45,705
How you gonna get home?

616
00:27:46,622 --> 00:27:48,166
I don't know.
I'll figure something out.

617
00:27:49,084 --> 00:27:51,461
But, uh, will you take my filing cabinet?

618
00:28:04,808 --> 00:28:07,227
[cell phone vibrating]

619
00:28:07,310 --> 00:28:08,603
Hey.

620
00:28:08,686 --> 00:28:11,647
[Randy] Hey.
So, uh, I've been thinkin' about it,

621
00:28:11,732 --> 00:28:14,901
and, uh, I feel bad
taking this check from you.

622
00:28:14,985 --> 00:28:17,028
Oh. Uh...

623
00:28:19,155 --> 00:28:20,240
Don't feel bad.

624
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:24,410
-You sure?
-Yeah, positive.

625
00:28:25,328 --> 00:28:26,579
Keep the check.

626
00:28:27,288 --> 00:28:28,749
As long as you're cool with it.

627
00:28:29,665 --> 00:28:32,085
So, uh, should I come over?

628
00:28:32,919 --> 00:28:34,420
Oh, um...

629
00:28:36,006 --> 00:28:38,383
maybe not, actually.

630
00:28:38,466 --> 00:28:43,221
I just had such a long day,
and I'm so tired. So...

631
00:28:43,304 --> 00:28:46,016
Yeah, no, no, that, uh...
that makes sense.

632
00:28:46,099 --> 00:28:48,351
Uh, I guess I'll talk to you tomorrow?

633
00:28:49,269 --> 00:28:50,937
Yeah. Definitely.

634
00:28:51,855 --> 00:28:54,149
Talk then. Bye.

635
00:28:57,068 --> 00:28:58,069
Bye.

636
00:29:38,026 --> 00:29:41,446
Elise, you've taught me
everything that I know.

637
00:29:42,613 --> 00:29:45,909
How to be a woman,
how to be a witch...

638
00:29:47,035 --> 00:29:48,786
even how to flirt with boys.

639
00:29:50,205 --> 00:29:51,622
Bobby never did ask me out,

640
00:29:51,706 --> 00:29:55,126
but... if he does,
you'll be the first one to know.

641
00:29:57,378 --> 00:29:58,713
Goodbye, my cousin.

642
00:29:59,672 --> 00:30:00,882
Goodbye, Elise.

643
00:30:02,926 --> 00:30:04,510
Goodbye, sweet witch.

644
00:30:07,013 --> 00:30:09,724
[speaking Latin]

645
00:30:14,187 --> 00:30:16,189
[in English] We are dust and shadow.

646
00:30:20,068 --> 00:30:22,737
And now, I must leave Witchita.

647
00:30:22,821 --> 00:30:25,073
I must leave home
and venture into the night

648
00:30:25,156 --> 00:30:28,284
with only my instinct
and my seven senses to protect me.

649
00:30:29,577 --> 00:30:30,703
Farewell, Elise.

650
00:30:31,704 --> 00:30:32,831
Farewell.

651
00:30:38,211 --> 00:30:40,213
[dramatic music playing]

